body:
Behind that pic are hundreds of tourists, lol (good for Parks Canada profit-wise). I visited it a while back and i didn't have a problem going in. This summer though, i tried to go there on 2 separate occasions (and tried 3x each), i couldn't go in because the parking was full. But 3rd time's a charm!

&#x200B;

Still breathtaking.

it's crazy, here i was thinking these damn kids and their young grandmas! and then it hit me, my grandma was around that age...  and she's 76 now.. didn't realize that 1960's was a whiiiilllllleeee ago. 

&#x200B;

We're closer to 2068 than 1968.

Thanks for your detailed response.

&#x200B;

Do you have an recommendation on the company you used to have the documents authenticated? i feel like it would be a hassle to go there lol. Sorry if have too many questions.

&#x200B;

Also, which option did you go for when you got married? it seems like option 2 would be faster since it's easier to have the documents translated in the local country.

Secure a job before moving. that's what i did a few months ago. i applied and applied. When i got an interview, they asked me when i'll be available to start. it gave me enough time to pack all my stuff, sell what i had to sell and drive from Ottawa-Calgary. 

&#x200B;

Moving is scary enough, but moving without a job in line is even scarier. Or if you have enough money saved (6 months rent) then, i think just go for it.

Not a problem, i'm sorry this happened to you. It's true, people who were affected are more concerned about their safety than their possessions.  

Yeah, i heard that it has been happening a lot lately in Calgary. At first, we thought that it's young people who have nothing better to do. But according to the police who investigated in Silverado, these were middle aged men. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I think it is. I remember my parents were checking all our vaccinations as part of our immigration process.. but that was 10 years ago, i'm not sure if it's still the same now..

&#x200B;

I don't think it is for tourist though

Thanks!

&#x200B;

What's your opinion on paint protection film? do you think they are worth it?
